BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Costa Brava//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Costa Brava — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Gamba de Palamós — The deep-water red prawn\, seared a minute with coarse salt\; suck the head.
DESCRIPTION:Say: GAM-ba de pa-la-MOSS. Landed and auctioned the same afternoon on the quay\; the town's name is on the label. Best: La Gamba\, Plaça de Sant Pere\, on the Palamós port — priced by weight
LOCATION:La Gamba\, Plaça de Sant Pere\, on the Palamós port — priced by weight
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Gamba+Placa+de+Sant+Pere+Palamos+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garoines — The violet sea urchin\, opened and eaten raw on toasted bread.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ga-roo-EE-ness. A cold-month food: the roe is fullest in late winter\; out of season\, do not order it. Best: The Palafrugell coves during the winter garoinada — the calendar card has the dates
LOCATION:The Palafrugell coves during the winter garoinada — the calendar card has the dates
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Calella+de+Palafrugell+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Anxoves de l'Escala — Anchovy cured for months in salt\, filleted by hand\, laid in oil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: an-SHOH-vess de les-KAH-la. Never cooked: on bread with tomato\, the coast's oldest preserved food. Best: Anxoves Solés\, L'Escala — buy the tins at the salter's own counter
LOCATION:Anxoves Solés\, L'Escala — buy the tins at the salter's own counter
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Anxoves+Soles+L%27Escala+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Suquet de peix — Monkfish\, scorpionfish and potatoes in a sofregit\, bound with a picada.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-KET de PESH. The boat stew made from the fish that would not sell. Best: Cal Tet\, L'Estartit — the catch off the Medes islands
LOCATION:Cal Tet\, L'Estartit — the catch off the Medes islands
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cal+Tet+L%27Estartit+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arròs a la cassola — Seafood rice in an earthenware pan\, made with the rice of Pals.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ah-ROSS a la ka-SSOH-la. The grain of the lower Ter holds its shape in the pot. Best: La Gamba\, Palamós — the rice of the port house\, for the table
LOCATION:La Gamba\, Palamós — the rice of the port house\, for the table
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Gamba+Palamos+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Peix i marisc a la planxa — The day's fish and shellfish\, raw or seared on the griddle\, with nothing else.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PESH ee ma-RISK a la PLAN-sha. The counter Ferran Adrià came back to\; ask the price by weight first. Best: Rafa's\, Carrer de Sant Sebastià\, Roses — five tables\, call ahead
LOCATION:Rafa's\, Carrer de Sant Sebastià\, Roses — five tables\, call ahead
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rafa%27s+Roses+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Guisats — Slow village stews of meat or game\, the plain's own cooking.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gee-ZATS. The Empordà eats inland as much as it eats fish. Best: Can Bonay\, under the arcades of Peratallada
LOCATION:Can Bonay\, under the arcades of Peratallada
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Bonay+Peratallada+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pa amb tomàquet — Bread rubbed with ripe tomato\, Empordà oil and salt.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PAM tu-MAH-ket. The base every anchovy and every slice of ham is laid on. Best: Any table in this guide\; at its best under an anchovy in L'Escala
LOCATION:Any table in this guide\; at its best under an anchovy in L'Escala
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=L%27Escala+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Coca d'anxoves — A flat oven bake under roasted vegetables or L'Escala anchovies.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KOH-ka dan-SHOH-vess. The village bakery's lunch\, eaten standing. Best: The bakeries of L'Escala\, round the salters' streets
LOCATION:The bakeries of L'Escala\, round the salters' streets
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=L%27Escala+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Recuit de drap — Fresh curd drained in its cloth\, with honey.
DESCRIPTION:Say: re-KWEET de DRAP. Keeps only a few days: eat it where it is made. Best: Mercat del Lleó\, Girona — the dairy stalls\, mornings
LOCATION:Mercat del Lleó\, Girona — the dairy stalls\, mornings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercat+del+Lleo+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panet — Artisan gelato slid into a warm brioche.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-NET. The way into the Roca universe without a booking. Best: Rocambolesc\, Carrer de Santa Clara\, Girona
LOCATION:Rocambolesc\, Carrer de Santa Clara\, Girona
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rocambolesc+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Un negre de l'Empordà — Garnatxa and Carinyena from old bush vines\, alone or blended.
DESCRIPTION:Say: NEG-ruh de lem-por-DAH. The red of the tramuntana country. Best: Espelt\, Vilajuïga — the estate's own reds\, by appointment\; or any table in this guide
LOCATION:Espelt\, Vilajuïga — the estate's own reds\, by appointment\; or any table in this guide
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Espelt+Viticultors+Vilajuiga+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garnatxa de l'Empordà — The sweet\, oxidative Garnatxa\, the coast's dessert wine.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gar-NAT-sha. The old farmhouse wine of the appellation\; have it with cheese or with recuit. Best: Mas Estela\, La Selva de Mar — by appointment\; or ask any table
LOCATION:Mas Estela\, La Selva de Mar — by appointment\; or ask any table
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mas+Estela+La+Selva+de+Mar+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cremat — Dark rum burned with sugar\, cinnamon and coffee\, served hot.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kruh-MAT. The havaneres' glass on the beach at Calella. Best: Calella de Palafrugell on the July havaneres night\; its card is in the glasses
LOCATION:Calella de Palafrugell on the July havaneres night\; its card is in the glasses
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Calella+de+Palafrugell+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:costa-brava-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ratafia — Green-walnut and herb liqueur\, sweet and bitter\, after lunch.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ra-ta-FEE-a. No two family bottles taste alike. Best: Ask for the house ratafia at the end of a meal in the tables
LOCATION:Ask for the house ratafia at the end of a meal in the tables
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Girona+Catalunya+Spain
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
